  "why": "I Became a Legend After My 10 Year-Long Last Stand, a 12 episode summer 2026 run airing 2026-07-03 to 2026-09-18 and still on air at labelling time. AniZip 19635 is the same run: SAME_AS ids to mal:62617 and anilist:199748 and the same episodeCount of 12. The Crunchyroll season GT00371671-GS00371672 is the same run: it maps SAME_AS onto all four members and its 11 episodes carry AniZip's episode titles in the same order, and its first episode on 2026-07-03 is the run's own start date. The JustWatch season 502870-532462 is the same run: it maps SAME_AS onto all four members and onto anizip:19635 and repeats the same 11 titles in order. AniZip episodes 1 to 10 pair with the Crunchyroll episodes on those exact non generic titles, from When I Returned Home, I'd Become a Hero to Storming the Enemy Position; the pairs rest on the titles, not the dates, because AniZip's slots run three days after Crunchyroll's (2026-07-06 against 2026-07-03 and so on), which is past a day of slack. All 11 Crunchyroll episodes pair with the JustWatch ones on the same titles, three of which JustWatch writes with a numeral (After 10 Years rather than After Ten Years) but is otherwise word for word. AniZip episode 11 (2026-09-14) carries only a Japanese title and episode 12 (2026-09-21) none at all, so neither is paired. Kitsu lists 22 untitled, undated episode rows against a 12 episode run, so nothing is asserted about them. The Netflix season 82941433-1 is left unsettled: its 11 episodes are titled Episode 1 to Episode 11, it carries no dates, and its count does not match the run's 12, so nothing but its own claim links it here."
